    <node id="NCMEC">
      <data key="d0">NCMEC</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC) is a private, nonprofit organization that serves as a vital clearinghouse for reports concerning child sexual abuse and exploitation. NCMEC plays a crucial role in receiving and processing reports of child sexual abuse material, which it may forward to law enforcement agencies, including federal law enforcement, as mandated by law. Additionally, NCMEC operates the CyberTipline, a dedicated platform for reporting instances of child sexual abuse content in the United States. Through these functions, NCMEC contributes significantly to the protection of children and the prevention of sexual exploitation.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC) serves as a clearinghouse for reports made under 18 U.S.C. §2258A, providing assistance to law enforcement agencies regarding child exploitation issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC) plays a role in handling reports of child sexual abuse content under various legal frameworks including 18 U.S.C. §2258A.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03af3b99beed5a891fbf02b542aed03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bddbca1d37abd901742b0ca6610124c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd054a4b792109f9e8db4282abab32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd865f79dca1f36757088e23e100d2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e37f622860a245462f05965e7b17dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0da0c71de54e74c0ac0187f2a193d2a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756583448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 U.S.C. §2258A">
      <data key="d0">18 U.S.C. §2258A</data>
      <data key="d1">legal_statute</data>
      <data key="d2">18 U.S.C. §2258A is a section of U.S. legislation that imposes mandatory reporting obligations regarding child sexual abuse content. It dictates the legal requirements for service providers to report instances of apparent child pornography and related information. This law specifically mandates that such reports be forwarded to the National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC). Additionally, 18 U.S.C. §2258A outlines the penalties for non-compliance, emphasizing the importance of timely and accurate reporting in combating child exploitation.&lt;SEP&gt;18 U.S.C. §2258A outlines the reporting and preservation requirements for visual depictions of apparent child pornography and related data by service providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03af3b99beed5a891fbf02b542aed03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bddbca1d37abd901742b0ca6610124c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd865f79dca1f36757088e23e100d2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e37f622860a245462f05965e7b17dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756583448</data>
    </node>
