    <node id="US law on reporting child sexual abuse content to NCMEC">
      <data key="d0">US law on reporting child sexual abuse content to NCMEC</data>
      <data key="d1">legal_statute</data>
      <data key="d2">The US law involves regulations regarding the reporting of child sexual abuse content to the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC).&lt;SEP&gt;US law establishes requirements for providers to report apparent child sexual abuse material to NCMEC, including specific data elements that must be included in such reports.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecd054a4b792109f9e8db4282abab32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd865f79dca1f36757088e23e100d2d</data>
