    </node>
    <node id="18 U.S.C. §2258A(a)(3)">
      <data key="d0">18 U.S.C. §2258A(a)(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This clause describes the geographic location information that should be provided in reports of child sexual abuse content.&lt;SEP&gt;This refers to a specific subsection of 18 U.S.C. §2258A that describes the requirement for geographic information related to the individual or website involved in child sexual abuse content cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e37f622860a245462f05965e7b17dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756580855</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 U.S.C. §2258A(a)(4)">
      <data key="d0">18 U.S.C. §2258A(a)(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This clause specifies that reports must include any visual depictions of apparent child pornography or related content.&lt;SEP&gt;This subsection of 18 U.S.C. §2258A mandates the inclusion of any visual depiction of apparent child pornography in reports.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e37f622860a245462f05965e7b17dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756580855</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 U.S.C. §2258A(a)(5)">
      <data key="d0">18 U.S.C. §2258A(a)(5)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This clause mandates the inclusion of complete communications containing visual depictions related to reports of child sexual abuse.&lt;SEP&gt;This describes the requirement for complete communication details, including visual depictions and attached files related to child sexual abuse content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e37f622860a245462f05965e7b17dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756580855</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 U.S.C. §2258A(c)">
      <data key="d0">18 U.S.C. §2258A(c)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">This clause establishes that NCMEC must make available reports made under subsection (a)(1) to federal law enforcement agencies.&lt;SEP&gt;This subsection discusses NCMEC's role in making reports available to federal law enforcement agencies following the reporting of child sexual abuse content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4e37f622860a245462f05965e7b17dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756580856</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 U.S.C. §2258A(f)">
      <data key="d0">18 U.S.C. §2258A(f)</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">This clause clarifies the limits of requirements on providers to monitor or search for child sexual abuse content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1756580366</data>
