    <edge source="NCMEC" target="18 U.S.C. §2258A">
      <data key="d6">35.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC) is tasked with processing reports made under 18 U.S.C. §2258A, which pertains to child sexual abuse content. As part of its mandate, NCMEC operates under the obligations set by this statute to handle such reports effectively. Additionally, NCMEC has a responsibility to make these reports available to law enforcement agencies, ensuring compliance with the requirements of 18 U.S.C. §2258A as it works to combat child exploitation.</data>
      <data key="d8">child protection,child safety,law enforcement collaboration,legal compliance,regulatory compliance,reporting agency,reporting framework,statutory obligation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-bddbca1d37abd901742b0ca6610124c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e37f622860a245462f05965e7b17dd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9a7654b3f51aa37fcdfbd958625cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcd865f79dca1f36757088e23e100d2d</data>
